SourceBench — Data Licensing and Terms of Use
=============================================

The code in this repository is MIT-licensed (see ../LICENSE). The data in this
directory is NOT uniformly licensed, because it mixes three kinds of material:
content we created, content derived from third-party research datasets, and
third-party web page content whose copyright we do not hold. Terms are stated
per component below.

CONTACT FOR CORRECTIONS AND TAKEDOWN REQUESTS
---------------------------------------------
Stephen Liu <xul052@ucsd.edu>
Requests for correction, attribution changes, or removal of stored page text
will be acknowledged and acted on at this address.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. data/content-scores/        LICENSE: CC BY 4.0
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Our evaluator's outputs: the eight-dimension scores (`content_vector`), the
written justifications (`content_vector_justification`), the intermediate
analyses (`group1_analysis` to `group3_analysis`), and the per-record metadata
(`query_id`, `agg_source_id`, `url`, `url_canonical`, `text_length`,
`query_type`).

These are our own generated content and are released under the Creative
Commons Attribution 4.0 International License.
    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

The justifications and analyses may quote short excerpts of the benchmark
queries and of the evaluated pages. Those excerpts remain subject to the terms
in sections 2 and 3(a), respectively.

This is the component the main source-quality metrics are computed from.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. data/queries/               LICENSE: per source dataset; see below
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
The 100 benchmark queries (`sourcebench_queries.csv`, `sourcebench_queries.jsonl`).
Terms follow each query's source dataset, given in the `source` field:

  - The 20 queries derived from HotpotQA, which is distributed under
    CC BY-SA 4.0, are released under CC BY-SA 4.0.
        https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
  - The other 80 queries are redistributed under the upstream terms listed
    below, for non-commercial research use with attribution to the original
    authors. We claim no license grant over them.

Provenance and upstream terms of the five source datasets:

  Source dataset          Queries   Upstream terms
  ----------------------  -------   ---------------------------------------
  HotpotQA                   20     CC BY-SA 4.0
  DebateQA                   20     No license specified by the authors
  Pinocchio                  20     No license specified by the authors
  Quora Question Pairs       20     Subject to Quora's Terms of Service
  VACOS NLQ                  20     Not confirmed; published at CHIIR '21
                                    (doi:10.1145/3406522.3446043)

DebateQA and Pinocchio state no license; queries derived from them will be
withdrawn on request from their authors. Pinocchio is itself derived from
FEVER, FEVEROUS, and PolitiFact, whose terms also apply upstream.

The license status of Quora Question Pairs and VACOS NLQ has not been
independently confirmed by us; users who intend to redistribute should verify
the upstream terms themselves.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. data/collected-sources/     LICENSE: layered; see below
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Frozen snapshots of the web pages cited by the evaluated systems, together
with the systems' own answers and our source-selection metadata. Three layers:

  (a) THIRD-PARTY CONTENT: the text and titles of the cited pages, i.e. every
      page-text field in `aggregated_sources` (`text_content` and its
      variants such as `old_text_content`, `text_content_w_short_links`, and
      `text_content_markdown_full_links`; `title`; `search_result_title`),
      and any page content returned inside the evaluated systems' API
      responses (`runs[].raw_response` and `runs[].search_results`, e.g.
      `results[].content` and `results[].raw_content` in the Tavily files).
      Copyright is retained by the respective publishers of those pages. We
      do not hold copyright in this material and grant no license over it.
      It is redistributed here solely to make the paper's evaluation
      reproducible without re-crawling a web that changes over time, for
      NON-COMMERCIAL RESEARCH USE ONLY.
      Any rights holder may request removal via the contact above; on such a
      request we will replace every stored copy of that page's text with its
      URL and a content hash.

  (b) `query_text`: derived from the source datasets in section 2 and
      governed by the same per-source terms.

  (c) Our added structure and metadata — `agg_source_id`, `frequency`,
      `ge_rank_list`, `ge_score`, `selected_topk`, `avg_ge_freq`,
      `domain_category`, `url_canonical`, the record layout itself, and the
      evaluated systems' responses as collected by us (excluding the page
      content covered by (a)): CC BY 4.0.

  Note: `search_result_date` and `search_result_last_updated` are dates
  reported by the page or the search provider. They are NOT crawl timestamps;
  this release does not record retrieval timestamps.

  Note: some files capitalize field names, e.g. `Aggregated_sources`,
  `Text_content`, and `Runs` in the Gensee and Perplexity files. The same
  terms apply regardless of capitalization.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. data/evaluation-results/, data/rank-scores/     LICENSE: CC BY 4.0
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Stored outputs of our analysis pipeline: overlap and rank metrics, per-source
and per-query-type scores, and collection reports. They hold URLs and values
we computed, and contain no stored page text. Some files repeat the benchmark
query text, which remains subject to the terms in section 2.
    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. NOT INCLUDED IN THIS RELEASE
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  - Human annotations (the 141-page annotated set, the 22-page calibration
    set, and per-annotator ratings). See the paper's reproducibility appendix.
  - Stored page texts for Claude-Sonnet-4.5. Its evaluator outputs, including
    the URL of every scored source, are in
    data/content-scores/claude-sonnet-4.5.json.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
6. CITING
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Attribution for the CC-licensed components is satisfied by citing the
SourceBench paper; see the Citation section of ../README.md.
